WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.080
Keanu Reeves is one of the world's most&nbsp;
beloved actors, known for his fantastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.840
work in action movies like The Matrix and the&nbsp;
John Wick series -- though his life has had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.360
its fair share of tragedies and hardships&nbsp;
that made him into the man he is today.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.920
The emotional gut-punches started at a&nbsp;
very young age for Keanu Reeves. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.680
just a 3-year-old kid when his father,&nbsp;
Samuel Reeves, abandoned the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.120
leaving his wife Patricia to raise&nbsp;
their two children alone. Predictably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.000
he and Keanu's relationship has devolved since&nbsp;
then, from rocky to completely nonexistent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.560
In the '90s, Samuel was arrested for possession&nbsp;
of cocaine and heroin and received a 10-year jail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.560
sentence. He's been out for a good while, but&nbsp;
his relationship with his son never recovered.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.240
Both men have commented on their falling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.280
out in the years since. Keanu&nbsp;
told Rolling Stone in 2000 -

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.080
"The story with me and my dad's&nbsp;
pretty heavy. It's full of pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.080
and woe and f---ing loss and all that s---."

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.680
Clearly, despite the fact that the two men&nbsp;
haven't spoken in years, the pain that lingers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.760
between them endures. Given how young Keanu&nbsp;
was when his father left the family, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.200
a whole lot of time he's had to spend dealing&nbsp;
with difficult feelings towards his father.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.160
For his part, Samuel told The Mirror -

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.360
"[Keanu's] made it clear that&nbsp;
he wants nothing to do with me."

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.320
He went on to add -

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.200
"I'm embarrassed by it all. Keanu said my life&nbsp;
was 'tragic' and, oh boy, does that hurt. Sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.880
yeah? I never figured things would end&nbsp;
up this way. But he'll always be my boy."

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.360
Reeves' newly single mother, Patricia,&nbsp;
moved frequently from state to state — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.840
marriage to marriage. Though&nbsp;
there's a lot of love there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.840
this sort of a constant upheaval is hard&nbsp;
for anyone to deal with — let alone a kid.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.160
After Reeves' father left, Patricia took the&nbsp;
little clan from Australia to New York City.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.040
Once settled in the Big Apple, she&nbsp;
met and married Broadway director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.880
Paul Aaron in 1970. The couple&nbsp;
moved to Toronto shortly after.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.120
Sadly, the romance didn't last, but, happily&nbsp;
enough, Aaron remained friendly with Reeves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.880
often giving him career advice and&nbsp;
helping him secure some early acting jobs.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.480
The Reeves family remained in the Yorkville&nbsp;
neighborhood of Toronto throughout much of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:49.920
1970s and into the following decade. In 1976,&nbsp;
Patricia married rock music promoter Robert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.560
Miller, but they unfortunately split in 1980.&nbsp;
Her next marriage, to hairdresser Jack Bond,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.960
lasted until 1994, by which time Reeves had&nbsp;
become an established force in Hollywood.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.440
As a kid, Reeves struggled academically,&nbsp;
attending four separate high schools in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.200
total. He never did earn his diploma,&nbsp;
and never pursued higher education.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.320
"Are you going to graduate?"

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.000
"Graduate?"

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.520
Reeves was, in fact, expelled from one of his&nbsp;
many schools. As he told the Daily Mail in 2008 -

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.840
"It was difficult. I went to four different high&nbsp;
schools in five years. I was OK academically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.640
good at English and creative&nbsp;
writing. I was on the chess team."

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.400
He added some reasons for the problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.400
including the size of the school and numerous&nbsp;
conflicts with students and staff, saying -

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.160
"I was one of those 'Why? kids — I asked&nbsp;
too many questions about everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.200
I couldn't stop even if it got me&nbsp;
into trouble. I wanted my autonomy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.320
and if you wanted to impose something on&nbsp;
me, then you and I would have a problem."

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.640
Still, he took the expulsion hard, saying -

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.160
"It's a terrible letter to receive, saying&nbsp;
you can't come back to school next year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.400
Getting asked to leave was very upsetting."

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.280
In the end, though, it inspired&nbsp;
him to get serious about acting.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.880
By the late '80s, Keanu Reeves was already&nbsp;
landing some major, enviable roles, most notably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.280
in the legendary goofball buddy comedy, Bill &amp;&nbsp;
Ted's Excellent Adventure. A few years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.600
he embraced mature films like 1990's I Love&nbsp;
You To Death and the following year's My Own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.560
Private Idaho, a drama about two street hustler&nbsp;
friends who embark on a journey of self discovery.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.960
Reeves became fast friends with his co-star in&nbsp;
those two films, River Phoenix. Phoenix was on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.840
a similar career trajectory to Reeves at the time,&nbsp;
having broken into serious roles in the late '80s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.520
Unfortunately, as is often the case with&nbsp;
young celebrities, Phoenix struggled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:29.280
the pressures of fame, and ultimately turned to&nbsp;
drugs. On October 31, 1993, tragedy struck when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.960
Phoenix collapsed outside Los Angeles' Viper Room&nbsp;
nightclub and died hours later at the age of 23.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.640
The tragedy stunned Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.040
and Reeves in particular. As Reeves&nbsp;
told the Guardian in 2019, Phoenix was -

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.120
"Definitely [one of] my closest friends from&nbsp;
that era. We shared an artistic sensibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.600
River was just so down-to-earth, spiritual&nbsp;
and a unique artist. Yeah, I miss him."

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.880
By the late '90s, Keanu had broken out of&nbsp;
rising-star status and become a bonafide leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.760
man. This happened largely on the backs of 1994's&nbsp;
Speed, in which he played a young cop trapped on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.720
a bus that's set to blow if it travels slower&nbsp;
than 50 miles per hour, and 1999's The Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.920
in which he played a man who discovers&nbsp;
the world around him is a simulation.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.360
It was around this time that he met and fell&nbsp;
in love with Jennifer Syme, an actress and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.640
personal assistant. Before long, Jennifer was&nbsp;
pregnant. However, shortly before Christmas, 1999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:20.560
Syme noticed she hadn't felt movement from the&nbsp;
baby in days. The two rushed to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.240
where ultrasound tests revealed that&nbsp;
the worst case scenario was indeed true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:30.080
Syme delivered their stillborn daughter, Ava&nbsp;
Archer Syme-Reeves, on December 24, 1999.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:35.520
Understandably, this loss devastated both parents.&nbsp;
As an anonymous friend told the Globe in 2000 -

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.160
"He really had his heart set&nbsp;
on becoming a dad. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.920
he and Jennifer are undergoing grief counseling&nbsp;
to try and help them cope with their anguish."

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:46.640
The loss of a child is one of the most intense&nbsp;
tragedies a person can endure. Inevitably, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:51.600
takes a massive toll on relationships — especially&nbsp;
the one between the child's parents. This was very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.080
much the case with Keanu Reeves and Jennifer&nbsp;
Syme. Sadly, but very much understandably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.400
the couple split a few weeks after laying&nbsp;
their daughter to rest in January 2000.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.520
Despite this, Reeves and Syme&nbsp;
remained close after the breakup.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.760
On April 1, 2001, Reeves met Syme at San&nbsp;
Francisco's Crepes on Cole, a popular brunch spot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.000
according to People. According to The Sun, she&nbsp;
attended a party at the home of Marilyn Manson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.320
that evening. For reasons unknown, after being&nbsp;
dropped off at her own home, she left again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.360
this time in her own vehicle. Shortly after 6&nbsp;
a.m. Syme's car slammed into a trio of parked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.840
cars — she wasn’t wearing a seatbelt and was&nbsp;
thrown from the vehicle. She died instantly.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.400
The tragedies of losing his child and former&nbsp;
partner changed Reeves forever. Years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.400
the grief still lay heavily upon&nbsp;
him. Reeves told Parade in 2006 -

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.960
"Grief changes shape, but it never ends. People&nbsp;
have a misconception that you can deal with it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.360
say, 'It's gone, and I'm better.' They're wrong.&nbsp;
When the people you love are gone, you're alone."

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.800
Keanu Reeves should've been enjoying&nbsp;
the peak of his acting career in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.800
late '90s and early aughts. However, the&nbsp;
nearly back-to-back losses he endured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.760
during this period cast a shadow&nbsp;
over just about everything he did.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.320
On top of that, his younger sister Kim&nbsp;
had been fighting leukemia since 1991.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.480
This long battle with cancer took an enormous&nbsp;
toll. Luckily, she had the support of her loved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.440
ones — including her big brother. According&nbsp;
to a 1999 article in Australia's Woman's Day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.320
Reeves supported her through the&nbsp;
years following her diagnosis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:16.800
sending flowers and special messages to his&nbsp;
sick sister at least once a week. Reeves said -

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.960
"I love Kim. She's so brave, and I want the&nbsp;
very best for her. You can star in hit movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.600
but that's nothing compared to going&nbsp;
through what Kim's been through."

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:27.760
Fortunately for everyone involved, Kim&nbsp;
Reeves went into remission in 1999.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:33.280
As the years went on, Reeves began taking on more&nbsp;
serious roles. The critics could be merciless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.840
Now, we'll admit, his attempt at an English accent&nbsp;
in 1992's Bram Stoker's Dracula is... not great.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.840
"I doubted everything, even my&nbsp;
mind. I was impotent with fear."

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:47.280
"I know."

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.040
But it, and other Reeves performances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.000
didn't merit the tidal wave of&nbsp;
mockery the actor soon faced.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Though the first Matrix movie was a hit,&nbsp;
the subsequent two were not as beloved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.160
Critics and fans alike began attacking what&nbsp;
they saw as Reeves' wooden underperformance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.800
as protagonist Neo. In his defense, most of the&nbsp;
main characters in the Matrix franchise have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.640
same deadpan expression, no matter what's&nbsp;
happening. But while Hugo Weaving gets to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:14.560
cackle and snarl as the villainous Agent Smith,&nbsp;
Reeves' Neo simply... doesn't emote. Ever. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:18.720
these years later, his infamously low-key&nbsp;
one-word catch phrase remains memorable.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.000
"...Whoa."

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.200
But that is, one can easily&nbsp;
argue, the point of the character.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.920
Luckily, Reeves has since found a&nbsp;
comfortable home in the excellent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.640
John Wick series, where his subtle&nbsp;
performance as the grief-stricken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.640
terrifyingly skilled protagonist makes&nbsp;
a lot of sense. Plus, you're too amazed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.920
by the incredible fight choreography to&nbsp;
really care much, one way or the other.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.320
Reeves is quite the philanthropist, although&nbsp;
he doesn't like to draw attention to this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.680
Regarding one of his charitable&nbsp;
projects, Reeves said in 2009 -

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.480
"I have a private foundation that's&nbsp;
been running for five or six years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.760
and it helps aid a couple of children's&nbsp;
hospitals and cancer research. I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:53.040
like to attach my name to it; I just&nbsp;
let the foundation do what it does."

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.840
In addition to his generosity, Reeves is also&nbsp;
shockingly private, largely shunning the flashy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.480
celebrity lifestyle. As a result of all this&nbsp;
generosity and humility, Reeves' reputation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:07.200
has drastically transformed in recent years. He's&nbsp;
gone from being dismissed as a moderately talented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:11.840
action star to a beloved figure of Hollywood.&nbsp;
All this sudden adoration might seem a bit much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.920
but it's not going anywhere any time soon.&nbsp;
The story of a man who's been through so much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.800
only to remain a generous, quiet person, is just&nbsp;
too wholesome for the internet not to fawn over.

